WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.761 --> 00:00:04.807
This guide shows how to prepare a work request on Android, review it

2
00:00:04.817 --> 00:00:07.473
on your computer, and check the saved result.

3
00:00:07.747 --> 00:00:09.487
We will go one step at a time.

4
00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:13.264
The people and records shown are fictional examples.

5
00:00:13.553 --> 00:00:15.209
Pause whenever you need more time.

6
00:00:18.583 --> 00:00:21.795
First, install the app for your device from this page.

7
00:00:22.056 --> 00:00:26.823
On Android, open Worker Demand and use the private login code given by

8
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:29.781
your Data Entry Operator, or DEO.

9
00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:36.934
On Windows or Linux, open VBGRAMG DEO Assistant and sign in with your

10
00:00:36.944 --> 00:00:38.101
own Google account.

11
00:00:38.389 --> 00:00:40.045
Keep login codes private.

12
00:00:43.361 --> 00:00:44.142
Step one.

13
00:00:44.403 --> 00:00:46.239
On your phone, open Home.

14
00:00:46.528 --> 00:00:50.156
Check the Panchayat or Village and the Financial Year.

15
00:00:50.431 --> 00:00:52.253
Use the area assigned to you.

16
00:00:52.514 --> 00:00:54.628
Then choose Create work request.

17
00:00:54.917 --> 00:01:00.240
If the area is wrong, ask your DEO to check your access before

18
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.031
you continue.

19
00:01:04.347 --> 00:01:05.114
Step two.

20
00:01:05.444 --> 00:01:08.212
Find a worker by name or Job Card.

21
00:01:08.486 --> 00:01:11.239
Tick the workers who belong in this request.

22
00:01:11.528 --> 00:01:13.684
Check their names and Job Cards.

23
00:01:13.972 --> 00:01:16.656
Look at the selected count before moving on.

24
00:01:16.944 --> 00:01:20.226
Only the workers you select belong in this request.

25
00:01:23.561 --> 00:01:24.523
Step three.

26
00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:28.231
Enter the requested days beside each worker.

27
00:01:28.519 --> 00:01:33.037
If everyone needs the same number, enter that number above Apply Days to

28
00:01:33.047 --> 00:01:35.606
All. Press Apply Days to All.

29
00:01:35.894 --> 00:01:39.203
Then check the number beside every selected name.

30
00:01:39.478 --> 00:01:42.773
Different workers can have different requested days.

31
00:01:46.081 --> 00:01:47.014
Step four.

32
00:01:47.303 --> 00:01:50.417
Choose Continue to open Work request details.

33
00:01:50.692 --> 00:01:53.848
Choose the Start Date and check the requested days.

34
00:01:54.094 --> 00:01:56.042
Read the other fields on this screen.

35
00:01:56.303 --> 00:01:58.931
Add a Work Code or Work Order when needed.

36
00:01:59.206 --> 00:02:02.320
Some requests allow these fields to stay empty.

37
00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:04.931
Follow the message shown in the app.

38
00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.148
Step five.

39
00:02:09.422 --> 00:02:11.162
Choose Review request.

40
00:02:11.436 --> 00:02:15.398
Read the area, worker names, days, and dates.

41
00:02:15.672 --> 00:02:17.787
Go back if anything needs changing.

42
00:02:18.075 --> 00:02:21.717
When the details are correct, choose Submit request.

43
00:02:21.992 --> 00:02:24.926
This sends the request to the office for review.

44
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.037
It does not create an official demand on the government website.

45
00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:33.364
Step six.

46
00:02:33.625 --> 00:02:36.045
Open History to follow the request.

47
00:02:36.306 --> 00:02:38.614
Read the status returned by the office.

48
00:02:38.889 --> 00:02:41.462
A draft saved on your phone stays on your phone.

49
00:02:41.722 --> 00:02:46.782
If a request is waiting for connection, reconnect and let the same request

50
00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:50.989
continue. Avoid creating another copy of the same request.

51
00:02:54.342 --> 00:02:55.762
The phone steps are complete.

52
00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:59.526
Now move to the D E O's Windows or Linux computer.

53
00:02:59.814 --> 00:03:04.707
The next lessons show how to review the request, check the workers, and

54
00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.873
choose whether to start official entry.

55
00:03:10.194 --> 00:03:11.101
Step seven.

56
00:03:11.389 --> 00:03:16.364
On your computer, open Notifications and choose Open request.

57
00:03:16.653 --> 00:03:21.003
You can also open Work Demand Management and choose Android requests.

58
00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.226
Open the request you want to review.

59
00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.739
Check who sent it and which area it belongs to.

60
00:03:30.047 --> 00:03:30.787
Step eight.

61
00:03:31.075 --> 00:03:37.093
Check the Panchayat or Village, Financial Year, Application Date, workers,

62
00:03:37.103 --> 00:03:38.301
and work dates.

63
00:03:38.575 --> 00:03:40.967
The received request keeps its own area.

64
00:03:41.256 --> 00:03:46.134
A different area selected for manual entry does not change this request.

65
00:03:46.408 --> 00:03:50.120
Correct any wrong details before going further.

66
00:03:53.447 --> 00:03:54.298
Step nine.

67
00:03:54.558 --> 00:03:56.395
Read Worked and Days left.

68
00:03:56.656 --> 00:04:01.173
Worked shows this worker's recorded days for the selected Financial Year.

69
00:04:01.447 --> 00:04:05.145
Days left is shared by everyone on the same Job Card.

70
00:04:05.419 --> 00:04:10.423
If two workers on one Job Card each show forty days left, that

71
00:04:10.433 --> 00:04:13.617
is one shared balance of forty, not eighty.

72
00:04:16.947 --> 00:04:17.742
Step ten.

73
00:04:18.031 --> 00:04:21.145
Read the saved checks beside each worker.

74
00:04:21.433 --> 00:04:25.770
Aadhaar shows whether the record says Aadhaar is available.

75
00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:29.520
eKYC is the electronic identity check.

76
00:04:29.794 --> 00:04:33.451
ABPS means Aadhaar Based Payment System.

77
00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.020
Check each answer.

78
00:04:35.294 --> 00:04:39.062
These saved answers may need updating before you continue.

79
00:04:42.361 --> 00:04:43.295
Step eleven.

80
00:04:43.569 --> 00:04:47.990
If an answer is old or missing, sign in to the official website

81
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.434
in the desktop Browser.

82
00:04:49.708 --> 00:04:52.087
Then choose Update worker checks.

83
00:04:52.375 --> 00:04:54.837
Read any warning beside the worker.

84
00:04:55.125 --> 00:04:56.809
A red mark needs attention.

85
00:04:57.056 --> 00:05:01.309
An unknown answer means the app does not have a usable saved answer.

86
00:05:01.569 --> 00:05:05.476
Saving an answer is separate from checking the website again.

87
00:05:08.761 --> 00:05:09.792
Step twelve.

88
00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:14.862
If needed, change the workers, requested days, or dates.

89
00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.612
Choose Save Changes.

90
00:05:16.886 --> 00:05:18.903
Review the saved details again.

91
00:05:19.192 --> 00:05:21.834
The original received list is kept.

92
00:05:22.108 --> 00:05:25.556
Saving changes does not start official entry.

93
00:05:25.844 --> 00:05:29.014
You will check the corrected request in the next step.

94
00:05:32.314 --> 00:05:33.484
Step thirteen.

95
00:05:33.758 --> 00:05:34.873
Choose Check demand.

96
00:05:35.161 --> 00:05:37.720
Read each message and the worker's name.

97
00:05:37.981 --> 00:05:40.387
Correct the details and check again.

98
00:05:40.661 --> 00:05:44.803
If you change a worker, a day, or a date after a check,

99
00:05:45.092 --> 00:05:46.581
run Check demand again.

100
00:05:46.869 --> 00:05:49.998
This check does not submit an official demand.

101
00:05:53.328 --> 00:05:54.456
Step fourteen.

102
00:05:54.744 --> 00:05:56.373
Wait for the check to pass.

103
00:05:56.633 --> 00:06:00.845
Review the workers, dates, and totals one last time.

104
00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:05.123
When you decide to continue, choose Submit to VBGRAMG.

105
00:06:05.411 --> 00:06:09.303
This starts entry on the official website through the desktop app.

106
00:06:09.578 --> 00:06:13.831
Read the next lesson before using the official website's buttons.

107
00:06:17.114 --> 00:06:21.451
Complete the official sign-in and enter the Security Code yourself.

108
00:06:21.739 --> 00:06:24.034
Keep your login details private.

109
00:06:24.308 --> 00:06:27.131
The official Proceed button can save a demand.

110
00:06:27.406 --> 00:06:32.229
If the website asks for a separate final Submit, review it and complete

111
00:06:32.239 --> 00:06:33.603
that action yourself.

112
00:06:33.878 --> 00:06:38.187
Do not assume that an unfinished final check means nothing was saved.

113
00:06:41.494 --> 00:06:42.484
Step fifteen.

114
00:06:42.758 --> 00:06:44.206
Read the result window.

115
00:06:44.481 --> 00:06:46.373
Look at Saved demands confirmed.

116
00:06:46.661 --> 00:06:49.123
Entry steps finished is a different count.

117
00:06:49.411 --> 00:06:53.984
If the final check is incomplete, choose Check saved results.

118
00:06:54.258 --> 00:06:58.456
This checks the saved result without sending the same demand again.

119
00:06:58.814 --> 00:07:02.442
Follow the message for any worker who still needs attention.

120
00:07:05.747 --> 00:07:06.820
That is the routine.

121
00:07:07.081 --> 00:07:10.626
On the phone, prepare, review, and send.

122
00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:16.584
On the computer, review the details, check the workers, and choose official

123
00:07:16.594 --> 00:07:19.723
entry. Finish by reading the saved result.

124
00:07:19.997 --> 00:07:23.542
Use Android History for the office's latest status.

125
00:07:23.817 --> 00:07:27.889
Repeat any lesson using the chapter buttons below this video.
